Sarah:A hundred percent yes so a lot of companies they&nbsp;have recently restructured their compensation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:28.240
or even the negotiation process. So typically there's always a range for compensation. And typically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:36.320
within that range, they break it up into three&nbsp;
tiers: so minimum, mid, and then max. For a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:42.080
of the time too for a recruiter, because the range&nbsp;
is so large from the minimum to the max&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:49.280
number, typically the range can be anywhere from&nbsp;
you know, $20k difference all the way to $100K&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.280
to $200k difference. And this is why a lot of&nbsp;
the time the recruiter will try to ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.480
you like "hey what are you looking for in terms of&nbsp;
compensation?" so they can gauge where can they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:06.800
